<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- Clutter has no analytics, advertising, tracking or crash-reporting code, and contacts no tracking domain. -->
  <key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
  <false/>
  <key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
  <array/>
  <!--
    What is declared as collected, and why (docs/privacy-audit-2026-11-06.md, docs/privacy-release.md). Notes, assets
    and settings stay on the device and are never transmitted, so none of that is declared. Two things go through
    Clutter's own Cloudflare Worker to Unsplash when the user searches for or picks a cover photo:

      Search History       the search text. The Worker keeps nothing; whether Cloudflare or Unsplash keeps it longer than
                           it takes to answer is not established (Unsplash's API terms say it may track searches), so
                           it is declared.
      Product Interaction  the report that a photo was picked or saved, which Unsplash's API guidelines require and
                           Unsplash records.

    Both are not linked to the user (Clutter has no account or identifier, and the Worker forwards none), are not used
    for tracking, and serve app functionality only. Images themselves load straight from Unsplash's image servers and
    from whatever host a note names, like any web page; that is not data Clutter or its code transmits, and is
    described in the privacy policy instead.
  -->
  <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
  <array>
    <dict>
      <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
      <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeSearchHistory</string>
      <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
      <false/>
      <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
      <false/>
      <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
      <array>
        <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
      </array>
    </dict>
    <dict>
      <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
      <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeProductInteraction</string>
      <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
      <false/>
      <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
      <false/>
      <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
      <array>
        <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
      </array>
    </dict>
  </array>
  <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
  <array>
    <!--
      File timestamps (stat, fstat, lstat): the modification and creation times of notes and assets are read to detect
      outside changes and to show a note's Created and Modified properties. Nothing leaves the device.
      3B52.1  files or folders the user granted access to (Spaces chosen or created through the system panel)
      C617.1  files inside the app's own container (recovery records, the parsed-note cache)
      DDA9.1  displayed to the person using the device (the Created and Modified properties)

      Not declared, on purpose, and checked against the built executable by scripts/verify-bundle.sh:
      disk space (no statfs, fstatfs, statvfs, fstatvfs or getattrlist import: the volume's type is read through the
      system's volume type-name value, ADR-069), system boot time (no mach_absolute_time; Rust's clock_gettime is not
      on Apple's list), user defaults, active keyboards.
    -->
    <dict>
      <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
      <string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp</string>
      <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
      <array>
        <string>3B52.1</string>
        <string>C617.1</string>
        <string>DDA9.1</string>
      </array>
    </dict>
  </array>
</dict>
</plist>
